% ============================================================================
% us-coins.query.adj — a worked recall over the kindergarten US-coins library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "how much is a quarter
% worth?": it states no money fact — it only `import`s the grounded table and
% asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the `coin_cents`
% rows and returns the value + the table's source/locator/trust. A token that is
% not a US coin abstains honestly — the engine never invents a value. The last
% query runs the relation BACKWARDS: given the value 5, recall the coin.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli us-coins.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "us-coins.adj"

? coin_cents(quarter, $Cents)      % expect 25
? coin_cents(dime, $Cents)         % expect 10
? coin_cents($Coin, 5)             % expect nickel — reverse lookup by value
? coin_cents(doubloon, $Cents)     % expect abstain — a doubloon is not a US coin
